      "title": "SP offers 26 seats to Congress for 2027 Uttar Pradesh Assembly polls",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/elections/assembly-election/sp-offers-26-seats-to-congress-for-2027-uttar-pradesh-assembly-polls-126112400397_1.html",
      "description": "Samajwadi Party secretary general Ram Gopal Yadav on Tuesday said the party has offered 26 seats to the Congress for the 2027 Uttar Pradesh Assembly elections, ahead of the second round of seat-sharing talks between the two parties.\nYadav, speaking to reporters before talks at Congress leader Pramod Tiwari's residence in Delhi, confirmed that 26 seats have been offered to the Congress.\n\"We have offered two seats which the Congress won, four seats where it finished second, and 20 other seats where we (SP) had secured 60,000-70,000 votes, while the Congress had received only around 2,000 votes,\" he said.\nUttar Pradesh Assembly has 403 seats.\nThe second round of discussions between the SP and Congress on seat-sharing is underway.\nReacting to the seat-sharing talks between the SP and Congress, Uttar Pradesh Minister Dayashankar Singh said in Ballia that the two parties were \"opposite poles\" and were coming together solely for their own interests.\nHe accused the SP chief Akhilesh Yada",
